<!DOCTYPE Bill PUBLIC "-//LSC//DTD Authoring Bill XML//EN" "l:\dtd\author\billauthoring.top"><Bill version="1.0" type="introLN" docName="S-0099.1"><IntroducedBillHeader><RequestNumber>H-0388.1</RequestNumber><BillNumber>HOUSE BILL 1206</BillNumber><StateLegSession><State>State of Washington</State><Legislature>59th Legislature</Legislature><Session>2005 Regular Session</Session></StateLegSession><Sponsors>Representative O&apos;Brien</Sponsors><IntroHistory><ReadDate>Read first time 01/18/2005.  </ReadDate><ReferredTo>Referred to Committee on Judiciary.</ReferredTo></IntroHistory></IntroducedBillHeader><BriefDescription>Repealing obsolete or superseded laws.</BriefDescription><BillBody><BillTitle><LineNumber line=" 1" page="1,1" hrt="no"/>	AN ACT Relating to repeal of obsolete or superseded laws; and<LineNumber line=" 2" page="1,2"/>repealing RCW 9.58.110, 9.58.120, 49.44.100, 67.14.020, 67.14.040,<LineNumber line=" 3" page="1,3"/>67.14.050, 67.14.060, 67.14.070, 67.14.080, 67.14.090, 67.14.100,<LineNumber line=" 4" page="1,4"/>67.14.110, 67.14.120, 70.54.060, and 70.54.065.</BillTitle><EnactingClause><LineNumber line=" 5" page="1,5" hrt="no"/>BE IT ENACTED BY THE LEGISLATURE OF THE STATE OF WASHINGTON:</EnactingClause><BillSection type="multiplerepeal"><LineNumber line=" 6" page="1,6" hrt="no"/><BegSecNew><NewSecText>NEW SECTION.</NewSecText><SecNum>Sec. </SecNum></BegSecNew><RCWSLText>The following acts or parts of acts are each<LineNumber line=" 7" page="1,7"/>repealed:<paraend/><LineNumber line=" 8" page="1,8" hrt="no"/>	<RepDecodParaCounter/> RCW <Cite>9.58.110</Cite> (Slander of woman) and 1909 c 249 s 181;<paraend/><LineNumber line=" 9" page="1,9" hrt="no"/>	<RepDecodParaCounter/> RCW <Cite>9.58.120</Cite> (Testimony necessary to convict) and 1927 c 90 s<LineNumber line="10" page="1,10"/>1 &amp; 1909 c 249 s 182;<paraend/><LineNumber line="11" page="1,11" hrt="no"/>	<RepDecodParaCounter/> RCW <Cite>49.44.100</Cite> (Bringing in out<hyphen/>of<hyphen/>state persons to replace<LineNumber line="12" page="1,12"/>employees involved in labor dispute<hardhyphen/><hyphen/>Penalty) and 2003 c 53 s 277 &amp;<LineNumber line="13" page="1,13"/>1961 c 180 s 1;<paraend/><LineNumber line="14" page="1,14" hrt="no"/>	<RepDecodParaCounter/> RCW <Cite>67.14.020</Cite> (Sale or other disposition of liquor<hardhyphen/><hyphen/>County<LineNumber line="15" page="1,15"/>license<hardhyphen/><hyphen/>Penalty) and 1873 p 437 s 2;<paraend/><LineNumber line="16" page="1,16" hrt="no"/>	<RepDecodParaCounter/> RCW <Cite>67.14.040</Cite> (Retail liquor license) and 1973 1st ex.s. c 154<LineNumber line="17" page="1,17"/>s 100, 1875 p 124 s 1, &amp; 1873 p 438 s 4;<paraend/><LineNumber line="18" page="1,18" hrt="no"/>	<RepDecodParaCounter/> RCW <Cite>67.14.050</Cite> (Wholesale liquor license<hardhyphen/><hyphen/>Billiard table,<LineNumber line="19" page="1,19"/>bowling alley licenses) and 1873 p 438 s 5;<paraend/><PageNumberFooter>		p. 1	HB 1206</PageNumberFooter><LineNumber line=" 1" page="2,1" hrt="no"/>	<RepDecodParaCounter/> RCW <Cite>67.14.060</Cite> (Liquor sales, keeping games, without license<hardhyphen/><hyphen eol="yes"/><LineNumber line=" 2" page="2,2"/>Penalty) and 1873 p 439 s 6;<paraend/><LineNumber line=" 3" page="2,3" hrt="no"/>	<RepDecodParaCounter/> RCW <Cite>67.14.070</Cite> (Purchase of license<hardhyphen/><hyphen/>Bond) and 1873 p 439 s 7;<paraend/><LineNumber line=" 4" page="2,4" hrt="no"/>	<RepDecodParaCounter/> RCW <Cite>67.14.080</Cite> (Duration of license) and 1873 p 439 s 8;<paraend/><LineNumber line=" 5" page="2,5" hrt="no"/>	<RepDecodParaCounter/> RCW <Cite>67.14.090</Cite> (Issuance of license) and 1873 p 439 s 9;<paraend/><LineNumber line=" 6" page="2,6" hrt="no"/>	<RepDecodParaCounter/> RCW <Cite>67.14.100</Cite> (When contrivance deemed kept for hire) and 1873<LineNumber line=" 7" page="2,7"/>p 440 s 10;<paraend/><LineNumber line=" 8" page="2,8" hrt="no"/>	<RepDecodParaCounter/> RCW <Cite>67.14.110</Cite> (Druggists excepted) and 1873 p 440 s 11;<paraend/><LineNumber line=" 9" page="2,9" hrt="no"/>	<RepDecodParaCounter/> RCW <Cite>67.14.120</Cite> (Disposition of fees, fines, and forfeitures)<LineNumber line="10" page="2,10"/>and 1987 c 202 s 226, 1969 ex.s. c 199 s 29, &amp; 1873 p 440 s 12;<paraend/><LineNumber line="11" page="2,11" hrt="no"/>	<RepDecodParaCounter/> RCW <Cite>70.54.060</Cite> (Ambulances and drivers) and 1945 c 65 s 1; and<paraend/><LineNumber line="12" page="2,12" hrt="no"/>	<RepDecodParaCounter/> RCW <Cite>70.54.065</Cite> (Ambulances and drivers<hardhyphen/><hyphen/>Penalty) and 1945 c 65<LineNumber line="13" page="2,13"/>s 2.</RCWSLText></BillSection><BillEnd>--- END ---<PageNumberFooter lastpage="yes">	HB 1206	p. 2	</PageNumberFooter></BillEnd></BillBody></Bill>